+# Hermes × Strata cache: owner GPU acceptance recipe (E5)
+
+Design: `H:\qwen38-v100\briefs\DESIGN-HERMES-CACHE.md` (user idea, Claude design).
+Status: `H:\qwen38-v100\briefs\REPORT-HERMES-CACHE.md` (implemented: Muse / reviewed: Sol).
+This recipe is the runnable form of the report's owner recipe. GPU measurements belong to the
+owner and have not been run here. E3's actual disk-persistence tests are deferred to E3.
+
+## Ground rules
+
+- Build with the exact `H:\qwen38-v100\scripts\build-strata-up.bat`. Same model/pack/numeric
+  flags across cached and cold runs. Isolated development engine at 18101 only.
+- Never touch production, deploy-strata, port 18100, or GPU clocks. Restart only the dev engine
+  when a case calls for it. Three repeats per case, unique result files per repeat.
+- Record per repeat: logs, timings, cache inventory, parity result, configuration identity.
+
+## True-cold flags
+
+Cold must disable every layer, not just the chain: `--prompt-cache 0 --tip-cache-gib 0
+--prompt-cache-root 0`. (`--prompt-cache 0` alone no longer suffices: root capture already
+requires prompt_cache > 0 in generate.cpp, `--tip-cache-gib 0` turns tips off while roots stay
+pinned, and `--prompt-cache-root 0` disables the root-pinning threshold.) When E3 lands, cold
+runs must also disable root-disk loading; if E3 ships enabled by default, it must provide an
+explicit disable flag and cold runs must pass it.
+
+## Cases
+
+1. Warm root + aux: fixed tools/system prefix session, then a title/aux request, then a second
+   session with the identical prefix and a different suffix. Require root reuse, second prefill
+   <= 2 s, and no tip from the aux request (main tip/root intact).
+2. Disk root (PENDING E3 - do not run yet): after root persistence completes, restart only the
+   dev engine with the same `--root-dir H:\qwen38-v100\strata-cache\roots`. New session on that
+   prefix must log `resume from root-disk` at the expected root length, prefill <= 5 s. In a
+   separate configuration, change one model/numeric identity field and confirm the
+   incompatible root file is ignored.
+3. Alternation and fork: parent -> isolated child (other root) -> parent, then parent -> forked
+   child -> parent. The fork prompt must carry the parent's generated assistant tool-call tokens
+   plus the tool result. Require the parent tip length to include generated tokens, tip reuse at
+   the longest matching prefix, suffix-only prefill (<= 3 s restore overhead + suffix cost), and
+   deterministic parity against cold output.
+4. Mixed correctness: cold run with the true-cold flags above; cached run with standard flags.
+   `python dev-18101/step3_validate.py capture --base-url http://127.0.0.1:18101 --label cold
+   --out <unique-cold.jsonl>`, same with `--label cached`, then `python
+   dev-18101/step3_validate.py compare --cold <cold.jsonl> --cached <cached.jsonl> --md
+   <unique-report.md>`. Require all 20 requests sane with token/output parity where applicable.
+   Include cvec/image identity boundaries and cancellation/recovery if supported.
+5. Speed: A/B `--spec-adapt` off/on x cache cold/warm for code, 12K, 40K shapes (same sampling
+   and length). Record resume source/k/suffix, restore/snapshot ms, prefill ms, decode tok/s,
+   acceptance. Decode must stay within measured run-to-run noise.
+6. Capacity/debug (GET/DELETE need S2; budget/eviction parts run now): lower the tip budget,
+   alternate enough lines to force eviction. Require pinned roots to survive, tip bytes within
+   budget, exact-prefix matching (two unrelated same-length lines must not cross-match), and the
+   disk dir within cap after background writes settle. After S2: GET `/v1/cache` inventory and
+   DELETE dropping non-pinned tips only. Record peak host RAM and retained lines; the fork
+   budget must hold at least depth+1 intended lines.
